  "slug": "sql-merge-bookings",
  "title": "Merge room bookings",
  "kind": "code",
  "language": "sql",
  "level": 5,
  "statement": "Table bookings(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, room TEXT, start_min INTEGER, end_min INTEGER), with start_min < end_min. A booking occupies its room from start_min (included) to end_min (excluded).\n\nFor each room, merge its bookings into busy blocks: two bookings of the same room belong to the same block when they overlap or when one ends exactly when the other starts, and this chains (if A joins B and B joins C, all three are one block). A block runs from the earliest start to the latest end of its bookings.\n\nReturn one row per block: room, block start, block end and the number of bookings in it. Sort by room, then by block start.\n\nOutput: columns room, block_start, block_end, bookings.\nConstraints: up to 20000 bookings, times from 0 to 200000. Bookings can be identical, and one booking can contain many later ones. Comparing every pair of bookings is too slow for the largest tests.\n\nExample\nbookings:\n  (1, 'A', 60, 120)\n  (2, 'A', 90, 150)\n  (3, 'A', 150, 180)\n  (4, 'A', 200, 230)\n  (5, 'B', 0, 300)\n  (6, 'B', 30, 60)\n  (7, 'B', 100, 120)\n  (8, 'B', 310, 320)\nOutput:\nA|60|180|3\nA|200|230|1\nB|0|300|3\nB|310|320|1",
  "starter_code": "-- Table: bookings(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, room TEXT, start_min INTEGER, end_min INTEGER)\nSELECT\n;\n",
  "time_limit_ms": 2000,
  "memory_limit_mb": 256,
  "comparator": "trim",
  "timer_seconds": 1800,
